      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, a new roof typically costs between\n\n$8,500 and $25,000 for a standard single-family home. The vast majority of Utah homeowners choosing standard architectural asphalt shingles pay an average of $11,000 to $16,500 for a complete tear-off and replacement.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $8,500 and $25,000"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The final price depends dynamically on the overall size of your home, the pitch (steepness) of the roof, and your chosen materials."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Home Size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most roofing contractors estimate pricing based on square footage or by a \"square\" (a 10x10-foot area). Below is the typical layout for standard asphalt architectural shingle installations in Utah:"
      },
